{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Jacob sent messengers.</b> As its Targum: איזגדין — emissaries." "<b>To the land of Seir.</b> For it originally belonged to Seir, and when Esau took Oholivamah as wife he inherited land in the land of Seir, for she was the daughter of Anah son of Tzivon son of Seir the Horite. And Esau would come and go there to his wives, and his heart was drawn after them, and it was called by his name 'the field of Edom.' Therefore he said to them 'field,' to inform you that his custom was in the field, for he is a hunter."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:00.261490153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}